WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.466
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book two.

2
00:00:05.766 --> 00:00:09.246
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.546 --> 00:00:15.066
Unit twelve: Money & Shopping. Today you will talk about money goals with the first conditional.

4
00:00:15.366 --> 00:00:18.262
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.653
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.517 --> 00:00:24.669
Allowance.

7
00:00:25.683 --> 00:00:28.472
Allowance means money parents give you regularly.

8
00:00:29.083 --> 00:00:31.350
I get a small allowance every week.

9
00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:34.370
Your turn. Say: Allowance.

10
00:00:37.233 --> 00:00:38.258
Allowance.

11
00:00:39.017 --> 00:00:39.832
Budget.

12
00:00:40.817 --> 00:00:43.048
Budget means a plan for how to spend money.

13
00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:45.383
I made a budget for this month.

14
00:00:45.983 --> 00:00:48.194
Your turn. Say: Budget.

15
00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:51.814
Budget.

16
00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:53.458
Save.

17
00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:56.612
Save means to keep money to use later.

18
00:00:57.217 --> 00:00:59.437
I save one thousand riel every day.

19
00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:02.215
Your turn. Say: Save.

20
00:01:05.067 --> 00:01:06.195
Save.

21
00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:08.195
Spend wisely.

22
00:01:09.183 --> 00:01:11.856
Spend wisely means to use money carefully.

23
00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:14.926
Spend wisely, and you won't run out.

24
00:01:15.517 --> 00:01:18.691
Your turn. Say: Spend wisely.

25
00:01:21.533 --> 00:01:22.976
Spend wisely.

26
00:01:23.717 --> 00:01:25.147
Impulse purchase.

27
00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:29.659
Impulse purchase means something you buy suddenly without thinking.

28
00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:32.308
That toy was an impulse purchase.

29
00:01:32.917 --> 00:01:35.685
Your turn. Say: Impulse purchase.

30
00:01:38.533 --> 00:01:40.022
Impulse purchase.

31
00:01:40.783 --> 00:01:41.993
Value for money.

32
00:01:42.983 --> 00:01:45.888
Value for money means good quality for the price.

33
00:01:46.483 --> 00:01:48.553
This bag is great value for money.

34
00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:51.884
Your turn. Say: Value for money.

35
00:01:54.733 --> 00:01:56.141
Value for money.

36
00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:57.884
Installment.

37
00:01:58.883 --> 00:02:02.055
Installment means one part of a payment paid over time.

38
00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:05.009
We pay for the phone in installments.

39
00:02:05.617 --> 00:02:07.886
Your turn. Say: Installment.

40
00:02:10.733 --> 00:02:11.955
Installment.

41
00:02:12.717 --> 00:02:13.695
Discount.

42
00:02:14.683 --> 00:02:17.089
Discount means a lower price than usual.

43
00:02:17.683 --> 00:02:19.973
The shop gave a 20% discount.

44
00:02:20.583 --> 00:02:23.212
Your turn. Say: Discount.

45
00:02:26.067 --> 00:02:26.859
Discount.

46
00:02:27.617 --> 00:02:28.989
Financial goal.

47
00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:32.796
Financial goal means something you save money for.

48
00:02:33.383 --> 00:02:35.662
My financial goal is a new bicycle.

49
00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:39.239
Your turn. Say: Financial goal.

50
00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:43.333
Financial goal.

51
00:02:44.083 --> 00:02:45.282
Expense.

52
00:02:46.283 --> 00:02:48.863
Expense means money you spend on something.

53
00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:51.322
Food is my biggest expense.

54
00:02:51.917 --> 00:02:54.790
Your turn. Say: Expense.

55
00:02:57.633 --> 00:02:58.762
Expense.

56
00:02:59.517 --> 00:03:00.448
Income.

57
00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:03.368
Income means money you receive.

58
00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:06.285
My income comes from selling drawings.

59
00:03:06.883 --> 00:03:09.222
Your turn. Say: Income.

60
00:03:12.067 --> 00:03:12.963
Income.

61
00:03:13.717 --> 00:03:14.880
Investment.

62
00:03:15.883 --> 00:03:19.090
Investment means money used to get more money or value later.

63
00:03:19.683 --> 00:03:21.822
Education is a good investment.

64
00:03:22.417 --> 00:03:24.848
Your turn. Say: Investment.

65
00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:28.898
Investment.

66
00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:33.595
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:36.798
Visal, how do you manage your allowance?

68
00:03:37.883 --> 00:03:42.231
I made a budget. I save half of it every week.

69
00:03:43.317 --> 00:03:45.049
What's your financial goal?

70
00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:50.613
A new bicycle. If I save money, I will reach my goal by June.

71
00:03:51.717 --> 00:03:53.600
What about impulse purchases?

72
00:03:54.717 --> 00:03:59.575
If I buy snacks every day, I won't have enough. So I spend wisely!

73
00:04:00.733 --> 00:04:02.396
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:05.911
Grammar focus: First conditional.

75
00:04:06.211 --> 00:04:07.479
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:08.183 --> 00:04:10.821
If I save money, I will reach my goal.

77
00:04:11.717 --> 00:04:14.018
If you spend wisely, you won't run out.

78
00:04:14.917 --> 00:04:17.125
If there is a discount, I will buy it.

79
00:04:18.067 --> 00:04:22.995
Use the first conditional for real possibilities in the future. Don't use 'will' after 'if'.

80
00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:27.807
Be careful! Don't say: If I will save money, I will buy a bike.

81
00:04:29.767 --> 00:04:32.207
Say: If I save money, I will buy a bike.

82
00:04:32.507 --> 00:04:34.658
Use the present simple after 'if'.

83
00:04:35.467 --> 00:04:37.840
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:38.633 --> 00:04:39.948
My Money Plan.

85
00:04:40.248 --> 00:04:43.397
I try to spend wisely and save part of my allowance.

86
00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:47.328
I write down every expense in a small budget book.

87
00:04:48.333 --> 00:04:51.482
My financial goal is to buy a new bicycle.

88
00:04:52.467 --> 00:04:56.231
If I avoid impulse purchases, I will reach my goal soon.

89
00:04:57.233 --> 00:05:00.800
If I find a good discount, I will get better value for money.

90
00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:05.751
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:06.617 --> 00:05:08.814
If I save money, I blank buy a bike.

92
00:05:09.114 --> 00:05:11.792
A, will. B, would. C, am.

93
00:05:15.333 --> 00:05:17.693
The answer is A: will.

94
00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:21.279
A plan for how to spend money is a blank.

95
00:05:21.579 --> 00:05:25.024
A, budget. B, discount. C, income.

96
00:05:28.567 --> 00:05:30.322
The answer is A: budget.

97
00:05:31.483 --> 00:05:34.284
Something you buy suddenly without thinking is an blank.

98
00:05:34.584 --> 00:05:38.679
A, impulse purchase. B, investment. C, installment.

99
00:05:42.233 --> 00:05:45.011
The answer is A: impulse purchase.

100
00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:49.212
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:52.398
How do you manage your allowance or pocket money?

102
00:06:01.183 --> 00:06:02.962
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:03.262 --> 00:06:11.023
I save half of my allowance in a box. If I save every week, I will have enough money for a new phone next year.

104
00:06:11.323 --> 00:06:12.928
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:13.817 --> 00:06:18.419
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and first conditional.

106
00:06:18.719 --> 00:06:23.311
Today's value is saving wisely. Save a little money and spend it carefully.

107
00:06:23.611 --> 00:06:26.542
See you in Unit thirteen. Goodbye!

108
00:06:26.842 --> 00:06:29.749
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

